  "verified": [
    "The raw native ListView suites keep lazy setup, selection and scroll behavior.",
    "No provider calls occur during one-million-row adoption. The 400x200 viewport requests fewer than 20 rows.",
    "The native owned getter transfers the exact allocation and byte count. xlang preserves NUL and UTF-8.",
    "The compatibility pointer getter and accessibility query keep their C-string behavior.",
    "Registration OOM preserves the old source, count and selection and releases the candidate.",
    "Provider source replacement and in-callback close do not publish stale text.",
    "Recursive owned provider reads report Busy, and native callers can handle that error.",
    "The owning callback retains its environment until physical return. Failed release clears the outputs.",
    "Provider errors reach both the checked direct read and the checked render boundary.",
    "Generated C directly calls native registration and retrieval, then adopts and validates the text.",
    "The beginner example produces visible glyph pixels on the real backend."
  ],
